{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395529169,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_029135014001LO8YMKdcWAtBsi","messageID":"msg_029134bfa001V9Jz9EOYWSCAOt","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"Now I need to understand the rules. Let me create a structured analysis. From the PACKET.md specification:\n\n1. **switch_inexhaustive**: A switch over a closed type where not all values are covered\n2. **unreachable_arm**: An arm that will never match because an earlier arm covers it\n3. **rebinding**: A pattern that repeats a bare name (introduces it twice)\n4. **return_not_declared**: A return type that doesn't match what's returned (from case c08)\n\nLet me look more carefully at what's expected. First, let me create a simple test to verify my understanding:","time":{"start":1787395526676,"end":1787395529163}}}
