{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395537413,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_0291363ac001T0XlR0QMWUaRf4","messageID":"msg_029135e96001ViaNlhyA1vrpLb","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"Let me trace through each case:\n\n**c01-exhaustive-closed/Verdict**: \n- Type State = :placed | :shipped | :lost (closed enum)\n- Covers all 3 cases\n- Expected: NOTHING (well-formed)\n\n**c02-catchall-open/Open**: \n- Parameter type is `atom s` (open type, not a closed enum)\n- Uses catch-all `_`\n- Spec says: \"A catch-all is legal only where the residual is open\"\n- Expected: NOTHING (well-formed)\n\n**c03-inexhaustive/Missing**: \n- Type State = :placed | :shipped | :lost (closed)\n- Only covers :placed and :shipped\n- Missing :lost\n- Expected: switch_inexhaustive\n\n**c04-unreachable/Shadowed**: \n- Type State = :placed | :shipped (closed)\n- Has `(true, _, _)` then `:placed` again \n- The third arm `:placed => :again` is unreachable (duplicate pattern)\n- Expected: unreachable_arm\n\n**c05-tuple-exhaustive/Decide**: \n- Parameters: bool ok, bool permanent, bool redelivered\n- All 8 cases covered by the patterns\n- Expected: NOTHING (well-formed)\n\n**c06-tuple-inexhaustive/Partial**: \n- Parameters: bool ok, bool permanent\n- Only covers (true, _) and (false, true)\n- Missing (false, false)\n- Expected: switch_inexhaustive\n\n**c07-guarded/Retry**: \n- Parameter type: int (unbounded)\n- `n when n < 5 => :retried` (n < 5)\n- `>= 5 => :exhausted` (n >= 5)\n- Together these cover all integers\n- Expected: NOTHING (well-formed)\n\n**c08-wrong-return/Wrong**: \n- Declared return type: `public int Describe`\n- But returns :placed (which is atom) and :gone (which is atom)\n- Not matching int\n- Expected: return_not_declared\n\nNow let me implement the checker. I'll use Python to parse and analyze the files:","time":{"start":1787395531693,"end":1787395537404}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787395573755,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"toolu_017pfgKw8DidA7d4BrAoAMST","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nswitchcheck: exhaustiveness and pattern checker for the B# language\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport re\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Set, Tuple, Optional\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom enum import Enum\n\n\nclass PatternType(Enum):\n    LITERAL = \"literal\"  # :atom or number\n    WILDCARD = \"_\"\n    VARIABLE = \"var\"\n    EQUALITY = \"==\"\n    RELATIONAL = \"relational\"  # >, <, >=, <=, and/or\n    TUPLE = \"tuple\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass TypeDef:\n    name: str\n    variants: List[str]  # For union types like :a | :b | :c\n\n\ndef parse_file(filename: str) -> Dict:\n    \"\"\"Parse a .bs file and extract relevant information.\"\"\"\n    with open(filename, 'r') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    result = {\n        'module': None,\n        'types': {},\n        'functions': [],\n        'errors': []\n    }\n    \n    lines = content.split('\\n')\n    \n    # Parse module name\n    for line in lines:\n        match = re.match(r'module\\s+(\\w+)', line)\n        if match:\n            result['module'] = match.group(1)\n            break\n    \n    # Parse type definitions\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(lines):\n        line = lines[i].strip()\n        match = re.match(r'type\\s+(\\w+)\\s*=\\s*(.+)', line)\n        if match:\n            type_name = match.group(1)\n            type_def = match.group(2).strip()\n            # Parse union type: :a | :b | :c\n            variants = [v.strip() for v in re.split(r'\\|', type_def)]\n            result['types'][type_name] = TypeDef(type_name, variants)\n        i += 1\n    \n    # Parse function signature and switch\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(lines):\n        line = lines[i].strip()\n        \n        # Match function signature: public <return-type> <name>(<params>)\n        sig_match = re.match(r'public\\s+(\\S+)\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\((.*?)\\)', line)\n        if sig_match:\n            return_type = sig_match.group(1)\n            func_name = sig_match.group(2)\n            params_str = sig_match.group(3)\n            \n            # Parse parameters\n            params = []\n            for param in params_str.split(','):\n                param = param.strip()\n                if param:\n                    parts = param.split()\n                    if len(parts) >= 2:\n                        param_type = parts[0]\n                        param_name = parts[1]\n                        params.append({'name': param_name, 'type': param_type})\n                    else:\n                        params.append({'name': param, 'type': None})\n            \n            # Find the switch statement\n            i += 1\n            while i < len(lines):\n                match_line = lines[i].strip()\n                \n                # Match clause head: FuncName(pattern) -> subject switch { ... }\n                clause_match = re.match(r'(\\w+)\\s*\\((.*?)\\)\\s*->\\s*(.*?)\\s+switch\\s*\\{', match_line)\n                if clause_match:\n                    subject_expr = clause_match.group(3).strip()\n                    \n                    # Parse switch arms\n                    arms = []\n                    i += 1\n                    while i < len(lines):\n                        arm_line = lines[i].strip()\n                        if arm_line == '}':\n                            break\n                        if arm_line and not arm_line.startswith('//'):\n                            # Match arm: pattern => result\n                            arm_match = re.match(r'([^=]+?)\\s*=>\\s*(.+)', arm_line)\n                            if arm_match:\n                                pattern = arm_match.group(1).strip()\n                                result_expr = arm_match.group(2).strip().rstrip(',')\n                                arms.append({\n                                    'pattern': pattern,\n                                    'result': result_expr\n                                })\n                        i += 1\n                    \n                    func_info = {\n                        'name': func_name,\n                        'return_type': return_type,\n                        'params': params,\n                        'subject': subject_expr,\n                        'arms': arms\n                    }\n                    result['functions'].append(func_info)\n                    break\n                \n                i += 1\n        \n        i += 1\n    \n    return result\n\n\ndef get_type_of_param(parsed: Dict, param_name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Get the declared type of a parameter.\"\"\"\n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return None\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    for param in func['params']:\n        if param['name'] == param_name:\n            return param['type']\n    return None\n\n\ndef parse_pattern(pattern: str) -> Dict:\n    \"\"\"Parse a single pattern and return its structure.\"\"\"\n    pattern = pattern.strip()\n    \n    if pattern == '_':\n        return {'type': PatternType.WILDCARD}\n    \n    if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n        # Tuple pattern\n        inner = pattern[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        return {\n            'type': PatternType.TUPLE,\n            'elements': [parse_pattern(e) for e in elements]\n        }\n    \n    # Check for guard\n    if ' when ' in pattern:\n        pattern_part = pattern.split(' when ')[0].strip()\n        guard_part = pattern.split(' when ')[1].strip()\n        return {\n            'type': 'guarded',\n            'pattern': parse_pattern(pattern_part),\n            'guard': guard_part\n        }\n    \n    # Check for relational pattern (>= 5, < 10, etc.)\n    if re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern):\n        return {\n            'type': PatternType.RELATIONAL,\n            'op': pattern.split()[0],\n            'value': int(pattern.split()[1])\n        }\n    \n    # Check for equality pattern (== name)\n    if pattern.startswith('=='):\n        name = pattern[2:].strip()\n        return {\n            'type': PatternType.EQUALITY,\n            'name': name\n        }\n    \n    # Check for atom literal\n    if pattern.startswith(':'):\n        return {\n            'type': PatternType.LITERAL,\n            'value': pattern\n        }\n    \n    # Check for number literal\n    if re.match(r'^-?\\d+$', pattern):\n        return {\n            'type': PatternType.LITERAL,\n            'value': int(pattern)\n        }\n    \n    # Variable/binding\n    return {\n        'type': PatternType.VARIABLE,\n        'name': pattern\n    }\n\n\ndef split_pattern_elements(s: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Split tuple pattern elements, handling nested tuples.\"\"\"\n    elements = []\n    current = []\n    depth = 0\n    \n    for char in s:\n        if char == '(' :\n            depth += 1\n            current.append(char)\n        elif char == ')':\n            depth -= 1\n            current.append(char)\n        elif char == ',' and depth == 0:\n            elements.append(''.join(current).strip())\n            current = []\n        else:\n            current.append(char)\n    \n    if current:\n        elements.append(''.join(current).strip())\n    \n    return elements\n\n\ndef extract_literals(pattern_dict: Dict, depth: int = 0) -> List:\n    \"\"\"Extract all literals from a pattern, returning possible values.\"\"\"\n    ptype = pattern_dict.get('type')\n    \n    if ptype == PatternType.WILDCARD:\n        return [None]  # Wildcard matches anything\n    \n    if ptype == PatternType.LITERAL:\n        return [pattern_dict['value']]\n    \n    if ptype == PatternType.VARIABLE or ptype == PatternType.EQUALITY:\n        return [None]  # Unknown value\n    \n    if ptype == PatternType.TUPLE:\n        elements = pattern_dict['elements']\n        result = [()]\n        for elem in elements:\n            elem_values = extract_literals(elem, depth + 1)\n            new_result = []\n            for r in result:\n                for v in elem_values:\n                    if isinstance(r, tuple):\n                        new_result.append(r + (v,))\n                    else:\n                        new_result.append((r, v))\n            result = new_result\n        return result\n    \n    if ptype == 'guarded':\n        # A guarded pattern only covers what the guard covers\n        return extract_literals(pattern_dict['pattern'], depth)\n    \n    return [None]\n\n\ndef get_all_variants(parsed: Dict) -> Optional[List]:\n    \"\"\"Get all variants of the input type, if it's a closed type.\"\"\"\n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return None\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    if not func['params']:\n        return None\n    \n    first_param = func['params'][0]\n    param_type = first_param['type']\n    \n    if param_type in parsed['types']:\n        type_def = parsed['types'][param_type]\n        return type_def.variants\n    \n    return None\n\n\ndef check_exhaustiveness(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check if the switch is exhaustive.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    subject = func['subject'].strip()\n    arms = func['arms']\n    \n    # Get the types of all elements in the subject\n    # If subject is just a variable name, it's the parameter\n    # If it's (a, b, c), it's a tuple of parameters\n    \n    subject_types = []\n    param_names = {}\n    \n    if subject.startswith('(') and subject.endswith(')'):\n        # Tuple subject\n        inner = subject[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        for elem in elements:\n            elem = elem.strip()\n            param_type = get_type_of_param(parsed, elem)\n            subject_types.append(param_type)\n            param_names[elem] = param_type\n    else:\n        # Single subject\n        param_type = get_type_of_param(parsed, subject)\n        subject_types.append(param_type)\n        param_names[subject] = param_type\n    \n    # Check if all subject types are closed\n    all_closed = True\n    for t in subject_types:\n        if t not in parsed['types']:\n            all_closed = False\n            break\n    \n    if not all_closed:\n        # If any type is open (like bare `atom`), catch-all is allowed\n        return errors\n    \n    # Get all possible combinations\n    all_variants = []\n    for t in subject_types:\n        if t in parsed['types']:\n            all_variants.append(parsed['types'][t].variants)\n        else:\n            return errors  # Open type\n    \n    # Generate all combinations\n    if len(all_variants) == 1:\n        all_cases = all_variants[0]\n    else:\n        # Cartesian product for tuples\n        import itertools\n        all_cases = list(itertools.product(*all_variants))\n    \n    # Check which cases are covered\n    covered = set()\n    has_catchall = False\n    \n    for arm in arms:\n        pattern = arm['pattern']\n        \n        # Check for catch-all\n        if pattern == '_':\n            has_catchall = True\n            break\n        \n        # Parse the pattern\n        parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern)\n        \n        # Extract literal values from pattern\n        literals = extract_literals(parsed_pattern)\n        \n        for lit in literals:\n            if lit is not None:\n                covered.add(lit)\n    \n    # If we're dealing with a single closed type, check coverage\n    if len(all_variants) == 1:\n        missing = []\n        for case in all_cases:\n            if case not in covered and not has_catchall:\n                missing.append(case)\n        \n        if missing:\n            errors.append('switch_inexhaustive')\n    \n    return errors\n\n\ndef check_return_type(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check if return expressions match declared return type.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    return_type = func['return_type']\n    \n    # Collect all return values from arms\n    for arm in func['arms']:\n        result = arm['result'].strip()\n        \n        # Determine the type of result\n        result_type = None\n        \n        if result.startswith(':'):\n            result_type = 'atom'\n        elif re.match(r'^-?\\d+$', result):\n            result_type = 'int'\n        elif result in parsed['types']:\n            result_type = result\n        # Could be more types, but focus on common ones\n        \n        # Check if it matches the declared return type\n        if result_type and result_type != return_type:\n            errors.append('return_not_declared')\n            break\n    \n    return errors\n\n\ndef check_for_rebinding(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check for rebinding errors (repeated variable names in pattern).\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    \n    # Get the clause head pattern\n    # For now, we're looking at the subject of the switch\n    # Rebinding would occur if a name is used twice\n    \n    # This needs more sophisticated parsing of the clause head itself\n    # For now, skip this check\n    \n    return errors\n\n\ndef check_unreachable(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check for unreachable arms.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    arms = func['arms']\n    \n    # Track which patterns we've seen\n    seen_patterns = set()\n    has_catchall = False\n    \n    for arm in arms:\n        pattern = arm['pattern'].strip()\n        \n        # Check for catch-all\n        if pattern == '_':\n            has_catchall = True\n            continue\n        \n        # For simple literal patterns, check if we've seen this exact pattern\n        # Parse the pattern to get its normalized form\n        parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern)\n        \n        # Convert back to a hashable form\n        pattern_key = normalize_pattern(parsed_pattern)\n        \n        if pattern_key in seen_patterns:\n            errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n            break\n        \n        seen_patterns.add(pattern_key)\n    \n    return errors\n\n\ndef normalize_pattern(pattern_dict: Dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Normalize a pattern to a hashable string for comparison.\"\"\"\n    ptype = pattern_dict.get('type')\n    \n    if ptype == PatternType.LITERAL:\n        return f\"lit:{pattern_dict['value']}\"\n    \n    if ptype == PatternType.TUPLE:\n        elements = pattern_dict['elements']\n        elem_strs = [normalize_pattern(e) for e in elements]\n        return f\"tuple:({','.join(elem_strs)})\"\n    \n    if ptype == 'guarded':\n        pattern_key = normalize_pattern(pattern_dict['pattern'])\n        return f\"guarded:{pattern_key}\"\n    \n    return str(ptype)\n\n\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: switchcheck <path-to-.bs-file>\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    filename = sys.argv[1]\n    \n    try:\n        parsed = parse_file(filename)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error parsing file: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    errors = []\n    \n    # Run all checks\n    errors.extend(check_exhaustiveness(parsed))\n    errors.extend(check_unreachable(parsed))\n    errors.extend(check_return_type(parsed))\n    errors.extend(check_for_rebinding(parsed))\n    \n    # Remove duplicates and print\n    unique_errors = sorted(set(errors))\n    for error in unique_errors:\n        print(error)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","time":{"start":1787395573628,"end":1787395573736}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_029137a02001DLJV0K9a3ulFCj","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","messageID":"msg_029135e96001ViaNlhyA1vrpLb"}}
