{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787395588485,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_0291441810019EzLjkZa3kGkv6","messageID":"msg_029143d21001JR97sEEhlEqYNX","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395592880,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_0291441830019FqdJC5UKxc2hZ","messageID":"msg_029143d21001JR97sEEhlEqYNX","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"The issue is that my unreachable detector is too naive. It's treating `(true, _, _)` and `(false, false, false)` as different because `_` isn't being normalized correctly. I need to rewrite this more carefully. Let me analyze the logic:\n\nFor c05:\n- (true, _, _) covers all (true, *, *)\n- (false, true, _) covers all (false, true, *)  \n- (false, false, false) covers (false, false, false)\n- (false, false, true) covers (false, false, true)\n\nTogether these cover:\n- true, *, * (8 cases)\n- false, true, * (4 cases)\n- false, false, false (1 case)\n- false, false, true (1 case)\n\nTotal: 8 + 4 + 2 = 14 but there are only 2^3 = 8 total cases! So the last arm is unreachable because (false, false, true) and (false, false, false) together are already covered by (false, false, *) which should be implied by the first three.\n\nWait, actually:\n- (true, _, _) = 8 cases\n- (false, true, _) = 4 cases  \n- (false, false, false) = 1 case\n- (false, false, true) = 1 case\n\nAll 8 = 2^3 are covered. So none is unreachable. My detector is broken.\n\nFor c06:\n- (true, _) covers all (true, *)\n- (false, true) covers (false, true)\n\nThis covers 2 + 1 = 3 of 4 cases. Missing (false, false).\n\nLet me rewrite with proper tuple coverage analysis:","time":{"start":1787395588483,"end":1787395592877}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787395598344,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01DNdkfZ3fT1uGrU4Cc3pKup","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/test_tuples.py << 'EOF'\n# Test coverage of tuple patterns\n\ndef covers_tuple(pattern, test_case):\n    \"\"\"Check if a pattern covers a test case.\"\"\"\n    if len(pattern) != len(test_case):\n        return False\n    \n    for p, t in zip(pattern, test_case):\n        if p == '_':\n            continue  # Wildcard matches anything\n        if p != t:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n# c05 patterns\npatterns = [\n    ('true', '_', '_'),      # (true, _, _)\n    ('false', 'true', '_'),  # (false, true, _)\n    ('false', 'false', 'false'),  # (false, false, false)\n    ('false', 'false', 'true'),   # (false, false, true)\n]\n\n# All bool combinations\nall_cases = [\n    (t, p, r) for t in ['true', 'false'] \n    for p in ['true', 'false']\n    for r in ['true', 'false']\n]\n\nprint(\"c05 coverage:\")\ncovered = set()\nfor i, pattern in enumerate(patterns):\n    for case in all_cases:\n        if covers_tuple(pattern, case):\n            covered.add(case)\n    print(f\"Pattern {i}: {pattern}\")\n    print(f\"  Covers: {[(j, all_cases[j]) for j in range(8) if covers_tuple(pattern, all_cases[j])]}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nTotal covered: {len(covered)} of {len(all_cases)}\")\nprint(f\"All cases covered: {len(covered) == len(all_cases)}\")\n\n# c06 patterns  \nprint(\"\\n\\nc06 patterns:\")\npatterns2 = [\n    ('true', '_'),      # (true, _)\n    ('false', 'true'),  # (false, true)\n]\n\nall_cases2 = [\n    (t, p) for t in ['true', 'false']\n    for p in ['true', 'false']\n]\n\ncovered2 = set()\nfor i, pattern in enumerate(patterns2):\n    for case in all_cases2:\n        if covers_tuple(pattern, case):\n            covered2.add(case)\n    print(f\"Pattern {i}: {pattern}\")\n    print(f\"  Covers: {[(j, all_cases2[j]) for j in range(4) if covers_tuple(pattern, all_cases2[j])]}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nTotal covered: {len(covered2)} of {len(all_cases2)}\")\nprint(f\"Missing: {[c for c in all_cases2 if c not in covered2]}\")\n\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/test_tuples.py\n"},"output":"zsh:1: operation not permitted: /tmp/test_tuples.py\n/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3: can't open file '/tmp/test_tuples.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory\n","metadata":{"output":"zsh:1: operation not permitted: /tmp/test_tuples.py\n/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3: can't open file '/tmp/test_tuples.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory\n","exit":2,"truncated":false},"title":"cat > /tmp/test_tuples.py << 'EOF'\n# Test coverage of tuple patterns\n\ndef covers_tuple(pattern, test_case):\n    \"\"\"Check if a pattern covers a test case.\"\"\"\n    if len(pattern) != len(test_case):\n        return False\n    \n    for p, t in zip(pattern, test_case):\n        if p == '_':\n            continue  # Wildcard matches anything\n        if p != t:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n# c05 patterns\npatterns = [\n    ('true', '_', '_'),      # (true, _, _)\n    ('false', 'true', '_'),  # (false, true, _)\n    ('false', 'false', 'false'),  # (false, false, false)\n    ('false', 'false', 'true'),   # (false, false, true)\n]\n\n# All bool combinations\nall_cases = [\n    (t, p, r) for t in ['true', 'false'] \n    for p in ['true', 'false']\n    for r in ['true', 'false']\n]\n\nprint(\"c05 coverage:\")\ncovered = set()\nfor i, pattern in enumerate(patterns):\n    for case in all_cases:\n        if covers_tuple(pattern, case):\n            covered.add(case)\n    print(f\"Pattern {i}: {pattern}\")\n    print(f\"  Covers: {[(j, all_cases[j]) for j in range(8) if covers_tuple(pattern, all_cases[j])]}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nTotal covered: {len(covered)} of {len(all_cases)}\")\nprint(f\"All cases covered: {len(covered) == len(all_cases)}\")\n\n# c06 patterns  \nprint(\"\\n\\nc06 patterns:\")\npatterns2 = 