{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395612344,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_029148ff5001uCPW7rp0yrGu7k","messageID":"msg_029148c3f001XXobsOGDwEv0V7","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"I can't use here-docs on this system. Let me think through this analytically:\n\nFor c05 with bool ok, bool permanent, bool redelivered (8 total cases):\n1. (T, _, _) covers: TTT, TTF, TFT, TFF = 4 cases\n2. (F, T, _) covers: FTT, FTF = 2 cases  \n3. (F, F, F) covers: FFF = 1 case\n4. (F, F, T) covers: FFT = 1 case\n\nTotal: 4 + 2 + 1 + 1 = 8 cases ✓ All covered, none unreachable.\n\nFor c06 with bool ok, bool permanent (4 total cases):\n1. (T, _) covers: TT, TF = 2 cases\n2. (F, T) covers: FT = 1 case\n\nTotal: 2 + 1 = 3 cases ✗ Missing: (F, F)\n\nSo my logic needs to:\n1. Parse tuple patterns correctly\n2. Build the coverage map properly\n3. Detect unreachable (covered by earlier pattern)\n4. Detect inexhaustive (not all cases covered)\n\nLet me rewrite with better tuple handling:","time":{"start":1787395608565,"end":1787395612337}}}
