{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395683155,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_02915ae9d001jdp7paEtYxeAy2","messageID":"msg_02915aa36001WjVqhWmLvZOakn","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"Aha! The issue is that `pattern_covers` is being called with a tuple (one-element) but the pattern is just a string. So when checking `:placed` against `(':placed',)`, the strings don't match because one is a string and the other is a 1-tuple. Let me fix the matching logic:","time":{"start":1787395681949,"end":1787395683149}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787395690678,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"toolu_01864WdUSACS3t7hbPXQES6T","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport re\n\ndef parse_pattern(pattern: str):\n    \"\"\"Parse a pattern and return its normalized form.\"\"\"\n    pattern = pattern.strip()\n    \n    if pattern == '_':\n        return '_'\n    \n    if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n        # Tuple pattern\n        inner = pattern[1:-1]\n        # Simple split - real version handles nesting\n        elements = [e.strip() for e in inner.split(',')]\n        return ('tuple', [parse_pattern(e) for e in elements])\n    \n    # Check for atom literal\n    if pattern.startswith(':'):\n        return pattern\n    \n    # Check for number literal\n    if re.match(r'^-?\\d+$', pattern):\n        return int(pattern)\n    \n    # Variable/binding\n    return pattern\n\n\ndef pattern_covers(pattern, value):\n    \"\"\"Check if a pattern covers a particular value.\"\"\"\n    if pattern == '_':\n        return True\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, str):\n        # Variable or atom literal\n        if pattern.startswith(':'):\n            # Atom literal - exact match only\n            return pattern == value\n        else:\n            # Variable matches any value (binding)\n            return True\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, int):\n        # Number literal\n        return pattern == value\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, tuple):\n        if pattern[0] == 'tuple':\n            # Tuple pattern\n            if not isinstance(value, tuple):\n                return False\n            patterns_list = pattern[1]\n            if len(patterns_list) != len(value):\n                return False\n            return all(pattern_covers(p, v) for p, v in zip(patterns_list, value))\n    \n    return False\n\n\n# Test single value\nprint(\"Test 1: Single values (not wrapped in tuple)\")\nvariants = [':placed', ':shipped', ':lost']\npatterns_from_arms = [':placed', ':shipped', ':lost']\n\ncovered = [False] * len(variants)\nfor pattern_str in patterns_from_arms:\n    parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern_str)\n    print(f\"Pattern: {pattern_str} -> {parsed_pattern}\")\n    \n    for i, case_value in enumerate(variants):\n        if pattern_covers(parsed_pattern, case_value):\n            covered[i] = True\n            print(f\"  Covers case {i}: {case_value}\")\n\nprint(f\"Covered: {covered}\")\nprint(f\"All covered: {all(covered)}\")\n\n# Test tuple values\nprint(\"\\n\\nTest 2: Tuple values\")\nall_cases = [('true', 'true', 'true'), ('true', 'true', 'false'), \n             ('true', 'false', 'true'), ('true', 'false', 'false'),\n             ('false', 'true', 'true'), ('false', 'true', 'false'),\n             ('false', 'false', 'true'), ('false', 'false', 'false')]\n\npatterns_tuple = [\n    ('tuple', [parse_pattern('true'), parse_pattern('_'), parse_pattern('_')]),\n    ('tuple', [parse_pattern('false'), parse_pattern('true'), parse_pattern('_')]),\n    ('tuple', [parse_pattern('false'), parse_pattern('false'), parse_pattern('false')]),\n    ('tuple', [parse_pattern('false'), parse_pattern('false'), parse_pattern('true')])\n]\n\ncovered = [False] * len(all_cases)\nfor pattern in patterns_tuple:\n    for i, case_value in enumerate(all_cases):\n        if pattern_covers(pattern, case_value):\n            covered[i] = True\n\nprint(f\"Covered: {covered}\")\nprint(f\"All covered: {all(covered)}\")\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/s9/s1jc1ww94kx0nhb3d33zxqrw0000gn/T/ringer-opencode-scratch.lytjgyAC27/opencode/debug.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/s9/s1jc1ww94kx0nhb3d33zxqrw0000gn/T/ringer-opencode-scratch.lytjgyAC27/opencode/debug.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"private/var/folders/s9/s1jc1ww94kx0nhb3d33zxqrw0000gn/T/ringer-opencode-scratch.lytjgyAC27/o