{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395856985,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_029184717001DRgMe6TnIUq8Jp","messageID":"msg_02918424c0019ailiKVw2jxAof","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"AH! There's the bug! `pattern_covers` is returning True for case `('false', 'true', 'true')` when given pattern `(true, _, _)`. The issue is that `'true'` (a variable) is matching anything!\n\nThe problem is that when I parse the pattern elements, I'm getting strings like `'true'` which are treated as variables, not as literals. But they should be literals. The issue is in my parse_pattern function - when I parse `'true'` as a pattern element, I need to check if it's a literal value for a bool type, not just treat it as a variable.\n\nBut wait, how do I know if it's a literal or a variable from just the string? In the language, literal values are lowercase identifiers or `:atom`. Variables are also lowercase identifiers. So I can't tell them apart just by looking at the string!\n\nLooking at c05 more carefully:\n\n```csharp\nRoute(o, p, r) -> (o, p, r) switch {\n    (true,  _,     _)     => :ack,\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThe clause head is `Route(o, p, r)` where `o`, `p`, `r` are variables. The switch subject is `(o, p, r)` which are the same variables. The patterns are `(true, _, _)` etc.\n\nIn the language, `true` and `false` are literal keywords (built-in values), not variables. So I should recognize them as keywords/literals, not as variables. Let me check the spec...\n\nThe spec shows:\n```csharp\nDecide(o, p, r) -> (o, p, r) switch {\n    (true,  _,     _)     => :ack,\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nSo `true` and `false` are being used as literal patterns. I should add them to my list of keywords/literals:","time":{"start":1787395852055,"end":1787395856977}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787395866191,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01Ed5nyxxMBhwKfetrMp3NYs","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"def parse_pattern(pattern: str) -> Union[str, Tuple, List]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse a pattern and return its normalized form.\n    Returns:\n    - '_' for wildcard\n    - ('tuple', [...patterns...]) for tuple patterns\n    - 'name' for variables\n    - ':atom' for atom literals\n    - number for number literals\n    - 'true' or 'false' for bool literals\n    - ('guarded', pattern, guard_str) for guarded patterns\n    - ('==', name) for equality patterns\n    \"\"\"\n    pattern = pattern.strip()\n    \n    if pattern == '_':\n        return '_'\n    \n    if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n        # Tuple pattern\n        inner = pattern[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        return ('tuple', [parse_pattern(e) for e in elements])\n    \n    # Check for guard\n    if ' when ' in pattern:\n        pattern_part = pattern.split(' when ')[0].strip()\n        guard_part = pattern.split(' when ')[1].strip()\n        return ('guarded', parse_pattern(pattern_part), guard_part)\n    \n    # Check for relational pattern (>= 5, < 10, etc.)\n    if re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern):\n        op = re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern).group(1)\n        value = int(re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern).group(2))\n        return ('relational', op, value)\n    \n    # Check for equality pattern (== name)\n    if pattern.startswith('=='):\n        name = pattern[2:].strip()\n        return ('==', name)\n    \n    # Check for atom literal\n    if pattern.startswith(':'):\n        return pattern\n    \n    # Check for bool literals\n    if pattern == 'true' or pattern == 'false':\n        return pattern\n    \n    # Check for number literal\n    if re.match(r'^-?\\d+$', pattern):\n        return int(pattern)\n    \n    # Variable/binding\n    return pattern","oldString":"def parse_pattern(pattern: str) -> Union[str, Tuple, List]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse a pattern and return its normalized form.\n    Returns:\n    - '_' for wildcard\n    - ('tuple', [...patterns...]) for tuple patterns\n    - 'name' for variables\n    - ':atom' for atom literals\n    - number for number literals\n    - ('guarded', pattern, guard_str) for guarded patterns\n    - ('==', name) for equality patterns\n    \"\"\"\n    pattern = pattern.strip()\n    \n    if pattern == '_':\n        return '_'\n    \n    if pattern.startswith('(') and pattern.endswith(')'):\n        # Tuple pattern\n        inner = pattern[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        return ('tuple', [parse_pattern(e) for e in elements])\n    \n    # Check for guard\n    if ' when ' in pattern:\n        pattern_part = pattern.split(' when ')[0].strip()\n        guard_part = pattern.split(' when ')[1].strip()\n        return ('guarded', parse_pattern(pattern_part), guard_part)\n    \n    # Check for relational pattern (>= 5, < 10, etc.)\n    if re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern):\n        op = re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern).group(1)\n        value = int(re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern).group(2))\n        return ('relational', op, value)\n    \n    # Check for equality pattern (== name)\n    if pattern.startswith('=='):\n        name = pattern[2:].strip()\n        return ('==', name)\n    \n    # Check for atom literal\n    if pattern.startswith(':'):\n        return pattern\n    \n    # Check for number literal\n    if re.match(r'^-?\\d+$', pattern):\n        return int(pattern)\n    \n    # Variable/binding\n    return pattern"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================