{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395911771,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_0291923f20017goCILYQhr4jam","messageID":"msg_029191fbc001145LwwPioDH0ZM","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"Perfect! All test cases pass as expected. Let me verify the implementation one more time by reviewing the key logic:\n\n1. **Exhaustiveness checking** (switch_inexhaustive):\n   - For closed types (bool, user-defined enums), we generate all possible values\n   - We check if all patterns together cover all values\n   - We flag an error if any value is not covered and there's no catch-all\n\n2. **Unreachability checking** (unreachable_arm):\n   - For closed types, we track which cases each arm covers\n   - If an arm only covers cases already covered by earlier arms, it's unreachable\n   - We report the first unreachable arm\n\n3. **Return type checking** (return_not_declared):\n   - We check if each return expression's type matches the declared return type\n   - We flag an error if any expression type doesn't match\n\n4. **Rebinding** (rebinding):\n   - Not yet implemented (needs clause head analysis, which is complex)\n\nLet me check the PACKET.md once more to see if there are any requirements I missed:","time":{"start":1787395908594,"end":1787395911768}}}
