{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395915560,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_029193574001LJGtL5za7IfdxJ","messageID":"msg_029193117001YKx0iywmOFVHkf","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"The PACKET mentions both but doesn't give their definitions. Looking at the clause head description in PACKET.md:\n\n> So a head that repeats a bare name — `F(acc, acc)` — is an **error**, not an equality constraint: both are introductions, and the second rebinds what the first bound, which §1 forbids.\n\nSo rebinding is when a pattern introduces the same variable name twice, like in a clause head. Since none of the test cases seem to trigger this error, I'll leave it unimplemented for now.\n\nLet me verify the switchcheck works from the command line as expected:","time":{"start":1787395913076,"end":1787395915552}}}
