{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787395919355,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_029194df5001A9Sied735k8PpY","messageID":"msg_029194908001VO1HoBm9z1HJS7","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395925578,"sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","part":{"id":"prt_029194df9001J5fXePCS4ze51e","messageID":"msg_029194908001VO1HoBm9z1HJS7","sessionID":"ses_fd6ecf8e7ffeQIAY4RnDqG5Oe6","type":"text","text":"Perfect! The implementation is complete and working correctly. Let me create a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented `switchcheck`, an exhaustiveness checker for the B# language that validates switch statements. The implementation:\n\n### Features Implemented\n\n1. **Exhaustiveness Checking** (`switch_inexhaustive`):\n   - Detects when a switch over a closed type (bool, user-defined enums) doesn't cover all possible values\n   - Recognizes catch-all patterns (`_`) as valid for open types (atom, int, etc.)\n   - Handles both single-value switches and tuple switches\n\n2. **Unreachability Checking** (`unreachable_arm`):\n   - Detects when a pattern in a switch arm will never match because earlier arms already cover all its cases\n   - Properly handles overlapping patterns in tuple switches\n\n3. **Return Type Checking** (`return_not_declared`):\n   - Verifies that all return expressions in switch arms match the declared return type\n   - Detects type mismatches (e.g., returning atoms when int is declared)\n\n4. **Pattern Parsing**:\n   - Supports literal patterns (:atom, true/false, numbers)\n   - Supports wildcard patterns (_)\n   - Supports tuple patterns ((a, b, c))\n   - Supports guarded patterns (n when n < 5)\n   - Supports relational patterns (>= 5, < 10, etc.)\n   - Supports equality patterns (== name)\n\n5. **Type System**:\n   - Recognizes built-in types: `bool` with values [true, false]\n   - Recognizes user-defined union types from type declarations\n   - Distinguishes closed types (finite enumerable values) from open types (infinite/unbounded)\n\n### Test Results\n\nAll 8 test cases pass:\n- ✓ Verdict: well-formed exhaustive switch\n- ✓ Open: catch-all on open type (valid)\n- ✗ Missing: reports `switch_inexhaustive` (missing :lost)\n- ✗ Shadowed: reports `unreachable_arm` (duplicate :placed)\n- ✓ Decide: well-formed exhaustive tuple switch\n- ✗ Partial: reports `switch_inexhaustive` (missing (false, false))\n- ✓ Retry: well-formed (open int type with complete coverage)\n- ✗ Wrong: reports `return_not_declared` (atom vs int mismatch)","time":{"start":1787395919353,"end":1787395925555}}}
