{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395950489,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"id":"prt_02919c2f3001y2W4FcF79oR00a","messageID":"msg_02919bee5001y9XR6UxVTt3h3F","sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","type":"text","text":"Let me start by implementing the rebinding check. The issue is in `n when n < 5`: the pattern `n` introduces a binding, and the guard `n < 5` uses that name again. This is rebinding.","time":{"start":1787395949299,"end":1787395950481}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787395957953,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01Dt7BiMzbLWYqCEGsFs3STL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","oldString":"def check_for_rebinding(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check for rebinding errors (repeated variable names in pattern).\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    # TODO: This requires analyzing the clause head pattern itself,\n    # not just the switch arms. For now, this is not implemented.\n    \n    return errors","newString":"def extract_names_from_pattern(pattern_str: str) -> Set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Extract all variable names introduced in a pattern.\"\"\"\n    names = set()\n    \n    # Remove guards for now - we'll check them separately\n    if ' when ' in pattern_str:\n        pattern_str = pattern_str.split(' when ')[0]\n    \n    pattern_str = pattern_str.strip()\n    \n    # Handle tuple patterns\n    if pattern_str.startswith('(') and pattern_str.endswith(')'):\n        inner = pattern_str[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        for elem in elements:\n            names.update(extract_names_from_pattern(elem))\n        return names\n    \n    # Skip wildcards\n    if pattern_str == '_':\n        return names\n    \n    # Skip literals\n    if pattern_str.startswith(':'):\n        return names\n    if pattern_str in ('true', 'false'):\n        return names\n    if re.match(r'^-?\\d+$', pattern_str):\n        return names\n    \n    # Skip relational patterns\n    if re.match(r'^(>=|<=|>|<)\\s*(-?\\d+)', pattern_str):\n        return names\n    \n    # Skip equality patterns\n    if pattern_str.startswith('=='):\n        return names\n    \n    # It's a variable name\n    names.add(pattern_str)\n    return names\n\n\ndef extract_names_from_guard(guard_str: str) -> Set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Extract all variable names used in a guard.\"\"\"\n    names = set()\n    # Simple approach: look for identifiers that are not operators/keywords\n    # Match word boundaries to get variable names\n    tokens = re.findall(r'\\b[a-zA-Z_]\\w*\\b', guard_str)\n    for token in tokens:\n        # Skip keywords and operators\n        if token not in ('and', 'or', 'not', 'when', 'true', 'false'):\n            names.add(token)\n    return names\n\n\ndef check_for_rebinding(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check for rebinding errors (repeated variable names in pattern or guard).\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    arms = func['arms']\n    \n    for arm in arms:\n        pattern_str = arm['pattern'].strip()\n        \n        # Extract names introduced in the pattern\n        introduced_names = extract_names_from_pattern(pattern_str)\n        \n        # Check if there's a guard\n        if ' when ' in pattern_str:\n            guard_part = pattern_str.split(' when ')[1]\n            guard_names = extract_names_from_guard(guard_part)\n            \n            # If any guard name was introduced in the pattern, it's rebinding\n            rebinding_names = introduced_names & guard_names\n            if rebinding_names:\n                errors.append('rebinding')\n                return errors\n    \n    return errors"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -542,15 +542,91 @@\n     \n     return errors\n \n \n+def extract_names_from_pattern(pattern_str: str) -> Set[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Extract all variable names introduced in a pattern.\"\"\"\n+    names = set()\n+    \n+    # Remove guards for now - we'll check them separately\n+    if ' when ' in patte