{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787395964901,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"id":"prt_02919ffdd001PPy86M4Y54kWpZ","messageID":"msg_02919fc16001HPpyp3ZslULsJN","sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787395966816,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"id":"prt_02919ffe20017GkGEO6sxe9OPg","messageID":"msg_02919fc16001HPpyp3ZslULsJN","sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","type":"text","text":"Great! Now let me mark that as completed and work on the == name coverage issue. The spec says:\n\n> \"A matched name credits nothing to the certain set either. Its value is unknown at compile time, so it may narrow what is *possible* and never counts as coverage — a `switch` whose only non-catch-all arm matches a name is inexhaustive over the whole subject type.\"\n\nSo `== name` patterns don't count toward coverage. Let me update the coverage logic:","time":{"start":1787395964898,"end":1787395966810}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787395975725,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01NjdiwDDq5WyD3Qx8a6akem","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","oldString":"def pattern_covers(pattern: Union[str, Tuple, List], value: Union[str, Tuple, List, int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if a pattern covers a particular value.\n    Returns True if the pattern matches the value.\n    \"\"\"\n    if pattern == '_':\n        return True\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, str):\n        # Check for literals first\n        if pattern.startswith(':'):\n            # Atom literal - exact match only\n            return pattern == value\n        elif pattern == 'true' or pattern == 'false':\n            # Bool literal - exact match only\n            return pattern == value\n        else:\n            # Variable matches any value (binding)\n            return True\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, int):\n        # Number literal - exact match\n        return pattern == value\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, tuple):\n        if pattern[0] == 'tuple':\n            # Tuple pattern\n            if not isinstance(value, tuple):\n                return False\n            patterns = pattern[1]\n            if len(patterns) != len(value):\n                return False\n            return all(pattern_covers(p, v) for p, v in zip(patterns, value))\n        \n        elif pattern[0] == 'guarded':\n            # Guarded pattern - we can't fully evaluate guards,\n            # but we can check the base pattern\n            return pattern_covers(pattern[1], value)\n        \n        elif pattern[0] == 'relational':\n            # Relational pattern - check the constraint\n            op, bound = pattern[1], pattern[2]\n            if not isinstance(value, int):\n                return False\n            if op == '>=':\n                return value >= bound\n            elif op == '<=':\n                return value <= bound\n            elif op == '>':\n                return value > bound\n            elif op == '<':\n                return value < bound\n        \n        elif pattern[0] == '==':\n            # Equality pattern - we can't evaluate this at static analysis time\n            # because it refers to a runtime value\n            return True  # Conservative: could match\n    \n    return False","newString":"def pattern_covers(pattern: Union[str, Tuple, List], value: Union[str, Tuple, List, int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if a pattern covers a particular value for COVERAGE analysis.\n    Returns True if the pattern definitely covers the value.\n    Note: == patterns return False because matched names don't credit to the certain set.\n    \"\"\"\n    if pattern == '_':\n        return True\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, str):\n        # Check for literals first\n        if pattern.startswith(':'):\n            # Atom literal - exact match only\n            return pattern == value\n        elif pattern == 'true' or pattern == 'false':\n            # Bool literal - exact match only\n            return pattern == value\n        else:\n            # Variable matches any value (binding)\n            return True\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, int):\n        # Number literal - exact match\n        return pattern == value\n    \n    if isinstance(pattern, tuple):\n        if pattern[0] == 'tuple':\n            # Tuple pattern\n            if not isinstance(value, tuple):\n                return False\n            patterns = pattern[1]\n            if len(patterns) != len(value):\n                return False\n            return all(pattern_covers(p, v) for p, v in zip(patterns, value))\n        \n        elif pattern[0] == 'guarded':\n            # Guarded pattern - we can't fully evaluate guards,\n            # but we can check the base pattern\n            return pattern_covers(pattern[1], value)\n        \n        elif pattern[0] == 'relational':\n            # Relational pattern - check the constraint\n            op, bound = pattern[1], pattern[2]\n            if not isinstance(value, int):\n                return False\n            if op == '>=':\n                return value >= bound\n            elif op == '<=':\n                return value <= bound\n            elif op == '>':\n                return value > bound\n            elif op == '<':\n                return value < bound\n        \n        elif pattern[0] == '==':\n            # Equality pattern - matched names don't credit to the certain set\n            # because their value is unknown at compile time\n            return False\n    \n    return False"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -235,10 +235,11 @@\n \n \n def pattern_covers(pattern: Union[str, Tuple, List], value: Union[str, Tuple, List, int]) -> bool:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Check if a pattern covers a particular value.\n-    Returns True if the pattern matches the value.\n+    Check if a pattern covers a particular value for COVERAGE analysis.\n+    Returns True if the pattern definitely covers the value.\n+    Note: == patterns return False because matched names don't credit to the certain set.\n     \"\"\"\n     if pattern == '_':\n         return True\n     \n@@ -287,11 +288,11 @@\n             elif op == '<':\n                 return value < bound\n         \n         elif pattern[0] == '==':\n-            # Equality pattern - we can't evaluate this at static analysis time\n-            # because it refers to a runtime value\n-            return True  # Conservative: could match\n+            # Equality pattern - matched names don't credit to the certain set\n+            # because their value is unknown at compile time\n+            return False\n     \n     return False\n \n \n","filediff":{"file":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","patch":"Index: /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -235,10 +235,11 @@\n \n \n def pattern_covers(pattern: Union[str, Tuple, List], value: Union[str, Tuple, List, int]) -> bool:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Check if a pattern covers a particular value.\n-    Returns True if the pattern matches the value.\n+    Check if a pattern covers a particular value for COVERAGE analysis.\n+    Returns True if the pattern definitely covers the value.\n+    Note: == patterns return False because matched names don't credit to the certain set.\n     \"\"\"\n     if pattern == '_':\n         return True\n     \n@@ -287,11 +288,11 @@\n             elif op == '<':\n                 return value < bound\n         \n         elif pattern[0] == '==':\n-            # Equality pattern - we can't evaluate this at static analysis time\n-            # because it refers to a runtime value\n-            return True  # Conservative: could match\n+            # Equality pattern - matched names don't credit to the certain set\n+            # because their value is unknown at compile time\n+            return False\n     \n     return False\n \n \n","additions":6,"deletions":5},"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","time":{"start":1787395975708,"end":1787395975709}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_0291a075d0014vQ05S4XWyekCc","sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","messageID":"msg_02919fc16001HPpyp3ZslULsJN"}}
