{"type":"text","timestamp":1787396080024,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"id":"prt_0291bb1de001C3nlW6HBniAk6M","messageID":"msg_0291badbf001kKfD8QflQHE0IR","sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","type":"text","text":"Perfect! All visible cases still pass. Now let me think about the held-out failures:\n\n- **h02-interval-gap**: My code should now detect gaps in relational patterns. For example, if you have `< 5` and `>= 6`, then 5 is not covered.\n- **h04-matched-name**: I now return False for == patterns, so a switch with only == patterns should be flagged as inexhaustive.\n- **h05-catchall-over-closed**: I check if a catch-all is over a closed type and if there are uncovered cases. If so, it's unreachable.\n\nLet me trace through h05-catchall-over-closed logic. A catch-all `_` over a closed type should be `unreachable_arm` if there are still uncovered cases. But actually, re-reading the spec:\n\n> \"A catch-all is legal only where the residual is open — over a `term`, or any type with an unbounded part. Where the compiler knows the remaining case names, `_` is an error\"\n\nSo a catch-all over a closed type is ALWAYS an error, not just when there are uncovered cases. Let me fix this:","time":{"start":1787396075998,"end":1787396080020}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787396093323,"sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_01LTZn4fRGbNpG3hy7bDdAKK","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","newString":"def check_unreachable(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check for unreachable arms.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    subject = func['subject'].strip()\n    arms = func['arms']\n    \n    # Parse subject types\n    is_tuple = subject.startswith('(') and subject.endswith(')')\n    subject_types = []\n    if is_tuple:\n        inner = subject[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        for idx, elem in enumerate(elements):\n            elem = elem.strip()\n            # Get type by position in function params\n            if idx < len(func['params']):\n                param_type = func['params'][idx]['type']\n            else:\n                param_type = None\n            subject_types.append(param_type)\n    else:\n        # Single subject - get type by position\n        if len(func['params']) > 0:\n            param_type = func['params'][0]['type']\n        else:\n            param_type = None\n        subject_types.append(param_type)\n    \n    # Check if all subject types are closed\n    all_closed = True\n    for t in subject_types:\n        if not is_closed_type(parsed, t):\n            all_closed = False\n            break\n    \n    if not all_closed:\n        return errors  # Can't analyze unreachable for open types\n    \n    # Generate all possible values\n    if is_tuple:\n        all_cases = generate_all_tuples(subject_types, parsed)\n        if all_cases is None:\n            return errors\n    else:\n        # Single type - don't wrap in tuple\n        all_values = all_values_for_type(parsed, subject_types[0])\n        if all_values is None:\n            return errors\n        all_cases = all_values\n    \n    # Track which cases are already covered\n    covered_cases = set()\n    \n    for arm_idx, arm in enumerate(arms):\n        pattern_str = arm['pattern'].strip()\n        \n        if pattern_str == '_':\n            # Catch-all over a closed type is always an error (unreachable)\n            # because the compiler knows all case names\n            if all_closed:\n                errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n            break\n        \n        parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern_str)\n        \n        # Find cases covered by this pattern\n        this_arm_covers = set()\n        for i, case_value in enumerate(all_cases):\n            if pattern_covers(parsed_pattern, case_value):\n                this_arm_covers.add(i)\n        \n        # Check if this arm is completely unreachable\n        # (all its cases were already covered by earlier arms)\n        if this_arm_covers and this_arm_covers.issubset(covered_cases):\n            errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n            break\n        \n        # Add this arm's cases to the covered set\n        covered_cases.update(this_arm_covers)\n    \n    return errors","oldString":"def check_unreachable(parsed: Dict) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Check for unreachable arms.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    \n    if not parsed['functions']:\n        return errors\n    \n    func = parsed['functions'][0]\n    subject = func['subject'].strip()\n    arms = func['arms']\n    \n    # Parse subject types\n    is_tuple = subject.startswith('(') and subject.endswith(')')\n    subject_types = []\n    if is_tuple:\n        inner = subject[1:-1]\n        elements = split_pattern_elements(inner)\n        for idx, elem in enumerate(elements):\n            elem = elem.strip()\n            # Get type by position in function params\n            if idx < len(func['params']):\n                param_type = func['params'][idx]['type']\n            else:\n                param_type = None\n            subject_types.append(param_type)\n    else:\n        # Single subject - get type by position\n        if len(func['params']) > 0:\n            param_type = func['params'][0]['type']\n        else:\n            param_type = None\n        subject_types.append(param_type)\n    \n    # Check if all subject types are closed\n    all_closed = True\n    for t in subject_types:\n        if not is_closed_type(parsed, t):\n            all_closed = False\n            break\n    \n    if not all_closed:\n        return errors  # Can't analyze unreachable for open types\n    \n    # Generate all possible values\n    if is_tuple:\n        all_cases = generate_all_tuples(subject_types, parsed)\n        if all_cases is None:\n            return errors\n    else:\n        # Single type - don't wrap in tuple\n        all_values = all_values_for_type(parsed, subject_types[0])\n        if all_values is None:\n            return errors\n        all_cases = all_values\n    \n    # Track which cases are already covered\n    covered_cases = set()\n    \n    for arm_idx, arm in enumerate(arms):\n        pattern_str = arm['pattern'].strip()\n        \n        if pattern_str == '_':\n            # Catch-all over a closed residual is an error (unreachable)\n            # because the compiler knows all remaining case names\n            if all_closed:\n                # Check if there are uncovered cases\n                if not all(i in covered_cases for i in range(len(all_cases))):\n                    # There are uncovered cases, so catch-all is unreachable\n                    errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n            break\n        \n        parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern_str)\n        \n        # Find cases covered by this pattern\n        this_arm_covers = set()\n        for i, case_value in enumerate(all_cases):\n            if pattern_covers(parsed_pattern, case_value):\n                this_arm_covers.add(i)\n        \n        # Check if this arm is completely unreachable\n        # (all its cases were already covered by earlier arms)\n        if this_arm_covers and this_arm_covers.issubset(covered_cases):\n            errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n            break\n        \n        # Add this arm's cases to the covered set\n        covered_cases.update(this_arm_covers)\n    \n    return errors"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -716,15 +716,12 @@\n for arm_idx, arm in enumerate(arms):\n     pattern_str = arm['pattern'].strip()\n     \n     if pattern_str == '_':\n-        # Catch-all over a closed residual is an error (unreachable)\n-        # because the compiler knows all remaining case names\n+        # Catch-all over a closed type is always an error (unreachable)\n+        # because the compiler knows all case names\n         if all_closed:\n-            # Check if there are uncovered cases\n-            if not all(i in covered_cases for i in range(len(all_cases))):\n-                # There are uncovered cases, so catch-all is unreachable\n-                errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n+            errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n         break\n     \n     parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern_str)\n     \n","filediff":{"file":"/private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","patch":"Index: /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n+++ /private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck\n@@ -716,15 +716,12 @@\n for arm_idx, arm in enumerate(arms):\n     pattern_str = arm['pattern'].strip()\n     \n     if pattern_str == '_':\n-        # Catch-all over a closed residual is an error (unreachable)\n-        # because the compiler knows all remaining case names\n+        # Catch-all over a closed type is always an error (unreachable)\n+        # because the compiler knows all case names\n         if all_closed:\n-            # Check if there are uncovered cases\n-            if not all(i in covered_cases for i in range(len(all_cases))):\n-                # There are uncovered cases, so catch-all is unreachable\n-                errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n+            errors.append('unreachable_arm')\n         break\n     \n     parsed_pattern = parse_pattern(pattern_str)\n     \n","additions":3,"deletions":6},"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/bsharp-audition/copilot-haiku45/switchcheck","time":{"start":1787396093298,"end":1787396093300}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_0291bc1960015Kw1MXSgCGdPWf","sessionID":"ses_fd6e692ddffeGvGNwVSLJa3nH7","messageID":"msg_0291badbf001kKfD8QflQHE0IR"}}
